WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

1. The Qurʾānic text itself, which carries no copyright.

2. The underlying work. Fī Riyāḍ Tafsīr al-Qurʾān al-Karīm is the tafsīr of
   Shaykh Ibrāhīm Niasse (d. 1975), compiled with footnotes by Muḥammad ibn
   Shaykh ʿAbd Allāh al-Tijānī al-Ibrāhīmī and printed by Majmaʿ al-Yamāma.
   This licence covers the transcription, translation, encoding and editorial
   work in this repository, not rights in the underlying text, which rest with
   their holders. Publication of the full Arabic commentary here was confirmed
   by the rights holder on 16 August 2026 (see CLAUDE.md).

3. Third-party texts presented for comparison: Tafsīr al-Jalālayn, Rūḥ al-Bayān,
   and any other work quoted under its own terms. A translation of al-Jalālayn
   by Feras Hamza (© 2007 Royal Aal al-Bayt Institute) was removed from the data
   in August 2026 and is not distributed here.

4. Vendored fonts and libraries, which carry their own licences.

THE SOFTWARE

This licence is deliberately the restrictive default, and it is a poor fit for
the code — CC BY-NC-ND forbids distributing a modified version, which is most of
what anyone would do with a Next.js application. If the site's code should be
reusable, relicense `src/`, `scripts/` and the build configuration under a
software licence (MIT and AGPL-3.0 being the usual two ends of that choice) and
leave CC BY-NC-ND over the edition's text. Until then, the terms above stand
over everything.

NO WARRANTY

This material is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The Qurʾānic
citations are machine-collated against a reference muṣḥaf and carry a status
mark; the verse numbering is Ḥafṣ-derived over a Warsh text and is a navigation
aid, not citation-grade. Verify against the printing before citing.
